  "next_candidate": "Evaluate a dedicated immutable inline Text payload without changing String, Attribute or Event maximum layout. This is a proposal only; no implementation in this experiment.",
  "recommendation": "Do not integrate the global inline String prototype: reference-heavy C parsing and the direct safe core regress despite fewer allocator calls.",
  "resource_tradeoffs": [
    "Inline bytes are part of their containing object; heap tracker accounts larger Parser/Vec allocations, while output and expansion byte limits remain unchanged.",
    "String and CString56->64, Attribute120->136, Event320->360, Parser1416->1456 on this x86_64 target.",
    "Raw pointers into inline buffers become invalid if their owning value moves; audited internal C callbacks retain stationary owners."
  ],
  "safety_review": [
    "No new unsafe storage mechanism; private Buffer preserves UTF-8 and terminal-NUL invariants.",
    "Inline growth uses originating selected allocator, commits only after successful allocation; heap clear retains capacity.",
    "All FFI string owners finalized before pointer capture; event attributes stay in fixed Vec slots during callback; callback-owned base snapshot survives SetBase.",
    "Content models borrow original str only while it remains alive, then copy names into one independently-owned C allocation.",
    "Independent root review found no blocker; ASan includes nested parsing/base replacement and 0/8/9 attribute arrays with22/23/24-byte values."
  ],
  "scope": "Isolated prototype based on source718 plus spare-NUL and stack-attribute-array optimization. No live runtime changes.",
  "validation": {
    "asan_ffi_unit_tests": 49,
    "asan_flags": "-Zsanitizer=address -Zexternal-clangrt -Clinker=clang -Clink-arg=-fsanitize=address",
